--!native
--[[
	Physics
	-------
	Client-side vehicle simulation. Successor to ADAPTTO; same model, same feel, tighter
	implementation.

	Model overview
	  * Ground contact: 33 raycasts per wheel sample the contact patch. The highest cluster
	    of hits (measured along the wheel's own up axis) gives the contact point and normal.
	    A spring-damper "sidewall" between the wheel and that point pushes the wheel up.
	  * Suspension: real Roblox constraints (struts, links, tie rods) built by Chassis.
	  * Tires: simplified Pacejka magic formula with load sensitivity and relaxation
	    lengths. Longitudinal/lateral forces are combined with a blend of the classic
	    friction-ellipse clamp and normalised combined slip (tunable).
	  * Tire load: static share + longitudinal and lateral load transfer from the measured
	    body acceleration (analytic, as in the original, now with lateral transfer).
	  * Drivetrain: engine (torque curve, friction, pumping, idle control, limiter, stall),
	    impulse-synchronising clutch, gearbox with torque cut while shifting, open/LSD/
	    locked axle and centre diffs, per-wheel spin integration with implicit tire damping
	    and static brake hold.
	  * Everything that couples wheel spin and tire force is sub-stepped at 240 Hz inside
	    one physics frame; the resulting tire force is the time average over the substeps,
	    so the impulse applied to the body matches what the wheels integrated.

	Timing
	  * PreSimulation: inputs, contact, tire/drivetrain integration, force output.
	  * RenderStepped: camera, wheel spin visuals, driver pivot, gauges, audio.
]]

